{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106835-technocratic-seeking","id":1106835,"title":"Technocratic Seeking.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-22T19:29:00-07:00","id":1106835,"title":"Technocratic Seeking.","content":"So, Technocrats have a bit of a rough time with their seekings. Given they don't actually have a codified system for them and it just kind of 'happens' over time.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to come up with a suitably impressive idea for a seeking for one of my characters, or at least the basics to run with. So far the idea is that in order to get through a shift at the construct, maintaining the cyborgs (BioMechanic Character.) they take a dose of Caffeine+. leading them to start seeing things. Both spirits and plain old fashioned hallucinations. After their shift is done they head on home but end up on a circuitous route back, while a hallucinatory version of their creator, a progenitor scientist, and their 'father' an Iterator talks to them.<br /> <br /> Does this sound like a decent idea for a seeking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T20:35:30-07:00","id":1106850,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm not thinking big enough, but I always envisioned them just having several late-night cram sessions/inventing sessions/experimentation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T22:41:40-07:00","id":1106891,"title":"","content":"They can do it through dreams. Dreams (to a Technocrat) are just unconscious processing, which may sometimes provide real insight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T06:36:17-07:00","id":1106992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OmegaZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106835-technocratic-seeking?p=1106850#post1106850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm not thinking big enough, but I always envisioned them just having several late-night cram sessions/inventing sessions/experimentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that they don't actually do it deliberately. There is no formal 'seeking' for technocrats which is one reason, by and large, they have fewer high Arete mages. Instead they generally stumble into something that becomes a seeking while doing something else. In this case, dosing an unstable stimulant to get through a long work shift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T07:27:31-07:00","id":1107008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106835-technocratic-seeking?p=1106992#post1106992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is that they don't actually do it deliberately. There is no formal 'seeking' for technocrats which is one reason, by and large, they have fewer high Arete mages. Instead they generally stumble into something that becomes a seeking while doing something else. In this case, dosing an unstable stimulant to get through a long work shift.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really agree with this. Technocrats, just like Traditionalists, still can have classic Seekings that happen in Mindscapes - they simply might consider them mere dreams or result of meditation...which is a thing they actually do, especially in NWO ranks.<br /> <br /> So, the end result might be a Technocrat waking up in a more or less refined 'Eureka!' moment, without considering what they went through being something metaphysical.<br /> <br /> But the process for both groups is very much the same - people with 'Circumspect Avatar' tend to have their seekings in the real world, people without tend to do them in mindscapes, with wiggle room in between. Wether or not the Mage in question sees a Seeking for what it truely is, is a different question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}